    {
      "id": "claim_e99fb05b388a4dafa1a051b18cd1adbe",
      "statement": "The client TYPERT_REMOTE descriptor and the host @Remote method are kept in sync by hand: each descriptor uses jsonParam to describe ordered position parameters (source 'json') and strictResult to describe the business return value, with ids of the form dsh-pet-panel#<namespace>/<method> and invocation { kind: 'direct' }. The full surface spans four namespaces: skillForge (list/read/write/delete/generate), toolIntegrations (list/read/write/delete), a2aConfig (get/setCard/upsertAgent/delete/checkAgents), and team (listTeams/createTeam/updateTeam/deleteTeam/listThreads/openThread/getThread/send). A mismatch between the @Remote signature and the manifest produces an ambiguous endpoint or a 'business result failed boundary validation' from the strict result codec.",
